<title>UK: Production of Nigerian Brass River crude normal-Agip.</title>
<headline>Production of Nigerian Brass River crude normal-Agip.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Production of Nigerian Brass River crude oil has not been affected by recent unrest and exports are flowing normally, said a source at Agip SpA, an equity producer of the crude.</p>
<p>&quot;Everything is normal. We have not been affected (by the unrest),&quot; the source said.</p>
<p>Current production of Brass River crude is about 170,000 barrel per days.</p>
<p>Nigerian oil production has been cut by 210,000 bpd from Bonny and Forcados fields after local villagers focred the closure of oil flow stations.</p>
<p>Operator Shell has sent a precautionary notice of possible force majuere on April loading of Bonny crude.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom 0171 542 4984</p>
</text>
